home = f'''<section class="hero-review"><div class="wrap hero-review-grid"><div><h1>Make 4853 an impartial vote.</h1><p class="hero-lead">Disclose interests. Finish internal DAO votes. Let every validator and token holder decide independently.</p><div class="action-row"><a class="button" href="#immediate">What needs to happen now {ARROW}</a><a class="button secondary" href="/voting/">Inspect the voting evidence</a></div><p class="hero-caveat">This review advocates a credible process—not YES, NO, or any person’s removal.</p></div><aside class="vote-deadline" aria-label="Proposal 4853 snapshot"><p class="status-live">Voting-period snapshot · 26 October</p><h2>4853 is still open.</h2><dl><div><dt>YES share, excluding abstain</dt><dd>41.62%</dd></div><div><dt>VETO share of all votes</dt><dd>32.57%</dd></div><div><dt>Current ballots captured</dt><dd>83</dd></div></dl><p>Voting ends <strong>31 October 2026, 03:40 UTC</strong>. Figures are a dated capture, not a live result.</p><a href="/voting/#tally">See the tally and scenario</a></aside></div></section>
<div class="wrap"><section class="section" id="immediate"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Before the vote closes</h2><p>Five concrete steps would make the result easier to trust, whichever way the vote goes.</p></div><ol class="action-list"><li><div><h3>Publish an interest register</h3><p>Directors, Think Tank members, ERIS signers, validators, large voting accounts and contractors should disclose relevant grant, payment, delegation, hosting and voting-contract interests at entity or handle level.</p></div><a href="/stakeholders/">See the relationships</a></li><li><div><h3>Declare contract voting intentions</h3><p>Publish the intended ampLUNA-hub and vAMP prop-gauge actions before those contracts vote. At capture, the gauge had zero votes and the hub had no native 4853 ballot.</p></div><a href="/voting/#contracts">How contract voting works</a></li><li><div><h3>Complete internal votes before validator ballots</h3><p>A validator following a DAO mandate should wait for that DAO’s final result. Lion DAO changed its native ballot while its own A33 vote remained open; both positions ultimately became YES.</p></div><a href="/voting/#lion-dao">Review the sequence</a></li><li><div><h3>Preserve independent ballots</h3><p>Validators and holders should vote on the proposal’s merits. A hub vote changes its native delegator power; it does not prove that validators share ownership or instructions.</p></div><a href="/voting/#counterevidence">Read the counterevidence</a></li><li><div><h3>Preserve the record for independent review</h3><p>Retain ballots, admin/configuration state, DAO messages, payment schedules and responses. Proposal 4853 itself calls for an impartial investigation; it does not predetermine liability.</p></div><a href="/evidence/">Open the evidence library</a></li></ol></section>
<section class="section section-grid"><div class="section-intro"><h2>What the evidence supports</h2><p>Credible governance questions, with limits stated beside each finding.</p></div><div class="finding-list"><article class="finding"><h3>Outcome-changing voting capability is concentrated</h3><p>A hypothetical full ampLUNA-hub YES would move the captured 4853 tally from failing to passing. One unattributed account can meet the vAMP participation quorum by itself.</p><p class="note"><strong>Not established:</strong> that either action has occurred, or that the large account is controlled by ERIS.</p><a href="/voting/#scenario">Test the scenario</a></article><article class="finding"><h3>Oversight participation and disclosure need review</h3><p>The Think Tank’s four substantive veto proposals received no YES or NO ballots. Members also have grant, payment or commercial relationships relevant to independence.</p><p class="note"><strong>Not established:</strong> deliberate inactivity, vote buying or common ownership.</p><a href="/stakeholders/#think-tank">Review all six members</a></article><article class="finding"><h3>The contract handover is incomplete</h3><p>ERIS proposal 9 transferred two CosmWasm upgrade admins to the Phoenix board. It did not change the hub’s stored owner or ICS20’s internal governance contract; wider Treasury/TLA roles also remain.</p><p class="note"><strong>Not established:</strong> exclusive key custody or the absence of any off-chain authorization.</p><a href="/governance/#handover">Compare admin and owner</a></article><article class="finding"><h3>Related-party payments need consistent controls</h3><p>Board beneficiaries participated in some payment decisions. Recurring contributor payments, related-party OTC trades and monthly validator-to-ERIS transfers require agreements, pricing and acceptance records.</p><p class="note"><strong>Not established:</strong> that gross funding is personal profit, or that every large transfer is compensation.</p><a href="/treasury/">Review payment categories</a></article></div></section></div>
<section class="counterband"><div class="wrap section-grid"><div><h2>A single-bloc theory does not fit the record.</h2></div><div><p>Smart Stake and Ceres voted <strong>NO WITH VETO</strong>; HighStakes voted <strong>ABSTAIN</strong>. Eleven reviewed allocation-linked validators had no current ballot. Directors have dissented on material proposals, and A272 failed.</p><p>These facts do not erase concentration or conflict concerns. They do require analysis that includes all stakeholders and alternatives.</p><a href="/stakeholders/">Review the whole stakeholder map {ARROW}</a></div></div></section>
<div class="wrap"><section class="section section-grid"><div class="section-intro"><h2>After 4853: make independence structural</h2><p>Short-term fairness needs longer-term controls.</p></div><div><ul class="reform-list"><li>Related-party disclosure, recusal and independent approval</li><li>A functioning Think Tank with notifications, complete messages and published rationales</li><li>Separate upgrade, configuration, treasury and voting powers with a verified handover</li><li>Transparent delegations, contract voting and validator mandates</li><li>Deliverable-based payments, OTC pricing review and independent reconciliation</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/governance/#reforms">Read the governance reforms and references {ARROW}</a></div></section></div>'''
